            standard grades. More importantly, premium fuel types exhibit wider IQRs, meaning consumers face
            less predictable pricing. The IQR for {largest_iqr_fuel} is
            <strong>{fmt_ppl(largest_iqr_val)} ppl</strong>, suggesting inconsistent pricing strategies or
            varying levels of competition in premium fuel markets.
        </p>
        <div class="policy-note">Policy implication: Regulators should examine whether premium fuel pricing is sufficiently transparent and whether consumers are adequately informed about the price differential versus standard grades.</div>
    </div>

